// U7 Final L4

::U7 Final L4 Q01::Which goal is SMART? {=For four weeks, average 7.5 hours of sleep on school nights using a nightly log.~Sleep more eventually.~Become perfectly healthy.~Never feel tired again.}

::U7 Final L4 Q02::Why record a baseline? {=It provides a starting point for judging change.~It guarantees improvement.~It replaces a goal.~It hides variation.}

::U7 Final L4 Q03::What is an adaptation trigger? {=A predefined condition that signals the plan should be reviewed or changed.~A punishment for missing one day.~A goal with no measure.~A reason to abandon monitoring.}

::U7 Final L4 Q04::Why consider nine wellness domains? {=Domains interact, so a plan should anticipate benefits and tradeoffs.~Every domain must receive identical time.~Only physical wellness can be measured.~Domains never affect one another.}

::U7 Final L4 Q05::A learner misses one planned walk. Best response? {=Review the broader pattern before deciding whether the plan needs revision.~Declare the entire plan failed.~Double every goal immediately.~Stop recording data.}

::U7 Final L4 Q06::Which indicator best matches a social-wellness goal? {=Number of planned supportive contacts completed each week.~Daily temperature outside.~Price of groceries only.~Hours of unrelated screen time.}

::U7 Final L4 Q07::A goal depends on equipment the learner cannot access. What should change? {=Revise the action step to an accessible alternative while preserving the purpose.~Keep the impossible action unchanged.~Remove all monitoring.~Blame motivation.}

::U7 Final L4 Q08::Why schedule review dates? {=Regular review turns observations into timely, evidence-based adjustments.~Review dates guarantee perfect results.~Plans should be changed every day.~Only final outcomes matter.}
